      "section_id": "methods_rl_rs_operator",
      "title": "Methods: RL-RS analytic-expansion operator",
      "status": "draft_ready",
      "draft_text": "Module2 is implemented as a learned analytic-expansion operator inside the existing Hybrid A* search loop. The operator is invoked only at the planner's analytic-expansion hook; it rolls out steering actions from the current search node, then accepts a shortcut only when the terminal Reeds-Shepp check certifies a collision-free connection to the goal. If this certificate is absent, the operator returns no shortcut and Hybrid A* continues primitive expansion. This section should therefore describe a planner-side analytic operator with fallback semantics, not a standalone global planner.",
